Subject: [PATCH] FatFile: mark a removed entry deleted before freeing its clusters

Not from upstream SdFat or crosspoint-reader: written for this fork to go
with 0003.

remove() freed the cluster chain and then marked the directory entry
deleted. With 0003, cacheSync() writes the FAT before the directory
sector, and with a separate FAT cache a dirty FAT sector can also be
evicted to the card while freeChain() walks a long chain. Either way the
freed clusters can reach the card while the entry still names them; a
power cut there leaves a live entry pointing at free clusters, and the
next allocation can hand them to another file (cross-linked files).

The entry is now marked deleted and written first, then the chain is
freed and synced. A power cut in between leaves allocated but
unreferenced clusters instead: lost clusters, which fsck reclaims.

---
--- a/src/FatLib/FatFileLFN.cpp
+++ b/src/FatLib/FatFileLFN.cpp
@@ -517,11 +517,6 @@
     DBG_FAIL_MACRO;
     goto fail;
   }
-  // Free any clusters.
-  if (m_firstCluster && !m_vol->freeChain(m_firstCluster)) {
-    DBG_FAIL_MACRO;
-    goto fail;
-  }
   // Cache directory entry.
   dir = cacheDirEntry(FsCache::CACHE_FOR_WRITE);
   if (!dir) {
@@ -537,11 +532,17 @@
   m_attributes = FILE_ATTR_CLOSED;
   m_flags = 0;
 
-  // Write entry to device.
+  // Write entry to device before freeing its clusters: a power cut in between
+  // leaves lost clusters, not a live entry pointing at free ones.
   if (!m_vol->cacheSync()) {
     DBG_FAIL_MACRO;
     goto fail;
   }
+  // Free any clusters.
+  if (m_firstCluster && (!m_vol->freeChain(m_firstCluster) || !m_vol->cacheSync())) {
+    DBG_FAIL_MACRO;
+    goto fail;
+  }
   if (!isLFN()) {
     // Done, no LFN entries.
     return true;
